@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<section class="ww-sec ww-sec-yellow ww-blog" id="cookies">
    <div class="ww-center">
        <p class="ww-kicker">Your choices</p>
        <h1>Cookies and privacy</h1>
        <p>This section is how cookies work on Wally Wombats today. The longer privacy notice follows underneath.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ww-cookie-copy">
        <h2>Cookie choices</h2>
        <p>A banner lets you accept all, reject all, or customize. The choice is stored in a first-party cookie named <code>ww_cookie_consent</code> for about a year. It is not sold, and other websites cannot read it. Cookie settings in the footer opens the banner again.</p>
        <p><button type="button" class="ww-btn ww-btn-navy" data-cookie-settings>Open cookie settings</button></p>
        <h2>Categories</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Necessary.</strong> Always on. Remembers this choice and keeps the site working. Google Consent Mode treats security storage as granted.</li>
            <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> Visit measurement. The site does not load Google Analytics or Tag Manager today. If a Google tag is added later, analytics storage stays denied until you allow this category.</li>
            <li><strong>Marketing.</strong> Advertising and remarketing. Ad storage, ad user data, and ad personalization stay denied until you allow this category. No advertising tag is installed today.</li>
            <li><strong>Media.</strong> YouTube, Spotify, Google Maps, and a TikTok embed script when a TikTok embed is on the page. Those stay unloaded until you allow media.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>What the pages load</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Before any Google tag, the page sets Google Consent Mode v2 defaults to denied, turns on ads data redaction, and updates the choice only after this cookie is read.</li>
            <li>Typefaces are files on this website. Visiting a page does not call Google Fonts.</li>
            <li>Blog stories are copied onto our pages by our server. Your browser does not load the Soro script. Story photos may come from the image host used for those articles.</li>
            <li>Booking, waivers, and social links (YouTube, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, Spotify) open those services only after you choose them.</li>
            <li>The contact form and mailing list send what you type to Wally Wombats. That is covered in the notice below.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Cookie choices on this section were updated November 15, 2026.</p>
    </div>
</section>
<partial name="_PrivacyPolicyBody" />
